WEBVTT

00:08.216 --> 00:11.386
You're resting your head on your face
and sighing like a girl who's in love.

00:11.469 --> 00:13.805
- Was I doing that?
- Yes, you were.

00:14.556 --> 00:15.557
Don't tell me

00:15.640 --> 00:18.393
there's been some development
with your ex-boyfriend.

00:19.728 --> 00:20.812
Well…

00:21.688 --> 00:23.815
I couldn't stop myself from saying…

00:23.898 --> 00:27.902
I'm sorry. I'm starting to like you again.

00:28.486 --> 00:31.156
Maybe I shouldn't have made a move?

00:31.239 --> 00:32.073
I see.

00:32.157 --> 00:35.577
So that's why you're eagerly
waiting for a reply, right?

00:44.711 --> 00:47.172
TAIGA: CAN I CALL YOU SOMETIME TODAY?

00:49.424 --> 00:50.675
I see.

00:51.551 --> 00:53.428
You made up with your girlfriend, huh?

00:54.304 --> 00:55.388
Yeah.

00:56.014 --> 00:59.017
So, regarding what you said the other day…

00:59.726 --> 01:00.810
I'm sorry…

01:02.228 --> 01:03.354
Okay.

01:04.647 --> 01:08.651
I was happy
that I won your approval, though.

01:12.447 --> 01:14.157
If this is the end,

01:14.240 --> 01:16.576
can't we have this conversation in person?

01:17.869 --> 01:21.081
Sorry, but I don't want to cause
my girlfriend any misunderstandings.

01:22.207 --> 01:24.459
You just dumped me,
so stop flaunting it in my face.

01:26.503 --> 01:27.504
But…

01:28.254 --> 01:29.297
I'm happy

01:30.089 --> 01:33.009
that you were able to keep
this precious girlfriend of yours.

01:34.135 --> 01:35.011
Yeah.

01:35.595 --> 01:36.930
Thanks for everything.

01:37.722 --> 01:39.057
No problem.

01:39.974 --> 01:42.185
Well, I still look forward
to working with you.

01:43.102 --> 01:44.270
Me too.

01:44.354 --> 01:45.480
Oh, Masumi.

01:48.149 --> 01:49.192
Happy New Year.

01:53.571 --> 01:54.697
Happy New Year.

02:10.755 --> 02:11.965
All right.

02:17.512 --> 02:18.346
I'M BACK TOGETHER WITH TAIGA!

02:18.429 --> 02:19.305
IT'S ALL THANK'S TO YOU, OPPA!

02:19.389 --> 02:20.265
I'LL TREAT YOU A BIG MEAL!
RIGHT, WE CAN SEE AT TANOMI!

02:20.348 --> 02:21.307
THANK YOU!

02:27.438 --> 02:28.731
I see.

02:31.025 --> 02:32.235
Congratulations, Rin.

03:36.549 --> 03:37.467
Visiting a shrine?

03:38.009 --> 03:40.970
Yeah, for hatsumode. Want to go together?

03:41.554 --> 03:44.015
What is "hatsumode"?

03:45.058 --> 03:48.853
You pray for happiness for the new year.

03:49.479 --> 03:51.189
I want to go with you.

03:51.272 --> 03:52.273
What do you think?

03:52.357 --> 03:53.399
That sounds like fun.

03:54.525 --> 03:56.152
That's settled then.

03:57.654 --> 04:01.407
Also, we're having a New Year's party
at Tanomi, so you should come too.

04:01.491 --> 04:02.533
There will be osechi too.

04:03.076 --> 04:04.410
- Osechi?
- Yeah.

04:04.494 --> 04:05.703
I've heard of that before.

04:08.873 --> 04:11.918
It's a meal you eat
during New Year's, huh?

04:13.169 --> 04:15.255
It'll be my first time. How exciting.

04:25.014 --> 04:26.140
What's wrong?

04:26.808 --> 04:30.061
I'm so happy
that I get to be with you again.

04:31.145 --> 04:33.731
Me too. I feel the same way.

04:33.815 --> 04:35.692
- Really?
- Yeah.

04:35.775 --> 04:36.943
Jinjja?

04:37.986 --> 04:39.028
Jinjja.

04:44.200 --> 04:45.410
Here you go.

04:47.287 --> 04:48.371
Here you go.

04:48.913 --> 04:50.331
All right.

04:50.415 --> 04:52.125
Osechi is so cute.

04:52.667 --> 04:54.085
Taiga and I made it together.

04:54.168 --> 04:55.670
It takes a lot of time and energy.

04:56.546 --> 04:59.090
It's like a work of art.
You really are a pro, huh?

05:00.008 --> 05:01.884
All right, eat up.

05:03.136 --> 05:04.804
Rin, you're not going back to Korea?

05:10.393 --> 05:12.103
Yeah…

05:13.104 --> 05:15.565
I'll be staying in Japan for now.

05:17.191 --> 05:20.778
That's not what I meant.
I was talking about the New Year's break.

05:21.738 --> 05:25.700
Oh, but I guess you celebrate
the Lunar New Year in Korea, right?

05:25.783 --> 05:26.826
Yes.

05:28.119 --> 05:29.454
What about you, Shige?

05:29.537 --> 05:30.413
Yeah…

05:30.496 --> 05:34.334
My sister is in the hospital,
so nobody will be home anyway.

05:34.417 --> 05:37.336
So I just delivered osechi
to her as a gift.

05:37.420 --> 05:38.421
I see.

05:39.255 --> 05:41.132
Anyway, go ahead and eat.

05:41.924 --> 05:42.925
Thanks for the food.

05:43.009 --> 05:44.594
Thanks for the food.

05:53.269 --> 05:55.313
These black soybeans are delicious.

05:56.022 --> 05:57.482
The black soybeans

05:57.565 --> 06:01.778
symbolize the desire to work
diligently throughout the new year.

06:01.861 --> 06:04.947
- Each osechi dish symbolizes something?
- Yes.

06:05.573 --> 06:09.160
Lotus roots
have holes that you can see through,

06:09.243 --> 06:11.662
so they symbolize having a bright future.

06:11.746 --> 06:13.331
How interesting.

06:17.543 --> 06:18.920
Happy New Year.

06:19.003 --> 06:20.296
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.

06:20.379 --> 06:22.090
Here, Noa, have a seat.

06:22.173 --> 06:23.508
Thanks.

06:23.591 --> 06:26.803
All right. Happy New Year.

06:26.886 --> 06:29.722
I look forward
to spending this New Year with you.

06:30.264 --> 06:31.682
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

06:32.266 --> 06:34.227
Eat the osechi with your mom.

06:34.310 --> 06:36.354
Thank you so much, Shige.

06:37.438 --> 06:38.898
I got my New Year's money.

06:38.981 --> 06:40.608
Good for you, Noa.

06:43.069 --> 06:44.445
New Year's is the best.

06:44.529 --> 06:45.530
Yeah.

06:46.489 --> 06:49.909
Speaking of which, do they give out money
on New Year's in Korea too?

06:50.493 --> 06:54.122
In Korea, if you do a "sebae" like this,
you get "don,"

06:54.205 --> 06:55.164
which means money.

06:55.248 --> 06:56.791
And so, we call it "sebaetdon."

06:58.126 --> 06:59.502
Sebaetdon?

07:00.128 --> 07:01.671
- Yeah, sebaetdon.
- Interesting.

07:02.255 --> 07:05.967
I like that system.
Maybe I should go around doing sebae?

07:06.050 --> 07:08.511
All you have been talking about is money.

07:08.594 --> 07:11.514
Well, I'm always the one
giving money to others.

07:11.597 --> 07:15.601
I don't get New Year's money
from my parents or my boyfriend.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.687
You've got to be kidding!

07:18.354 --> 07:20.648
40,000 just in one morning?

07:22.316 --> 07:25.528
Akinori, we're getting lunch.
Want to come?

07:26.404 --> 07:28.739
I'll keep at it.

07:30.324 --> 07:33.077
You should take a breather
and start fresh.

07:34.203 --> 07:36.873
Plus, I want to let you in on a nice deal.

07:40.835 --> 07:44.130
Investment?
So that really is profitable, huh?

07:44.213 --> 07:45.465
It's a pretty sweet deal.

07:46.257 --> 07:49.802
You can expect 200,000 a month
in dividends.

07:49.886 --> 07:51.387
It's a solid investment.

07:51.471 --> 07:52.722
200,000 a month?

07:53.681 --> 07:55.141
That sounds like a dream.

07:55.725 --> 07:57.768
We can make bank through investments

07:58.519 --> 07:59.562
and relax and have fun.

08:05.109 --> 08:06.360
But…

08:07.361 --> 08:10.490
I need 500,000 to start, huh?

08:14.160 --> 08:16.245
If you're going to hesitate, back out.

08:16.329 --> 08:19.457
Do you understand how lucky you are
that Zaki is letting you in on this?

08:19.540 --> 08:22.585
No, no! I'm really grateful! I'm sorry.

08:25.129 --> 08:26.130
Um…

08:27.590 --> 08:30.092
When do I need the money by,
in order to join?

08:31.969 --> 08:34.931
The cutoff
is at the beginning of next week,

08:35.014 --> 08:37.934
so three days is all I can wait.

08:39.602 --> 08:40.937
Three days?

08:47.985 --> 08:50.196
This is the best. It's so delicious.

08:50.279 --> 08:52.698
Noa, you're drinking too fast.

08:52.782 --> 08:54.033
It's fine.

08:54.116 --> 08:56.160
I'm so happy.

08:57.662 --> 09:00.122
This year is looking promising.

09:01.040 --> 09:02.416
You're drinking too much.

09:03.084 --> 09:03.918
Shut up.

09:04.001 --> 09:09.215
HAPPY NEW YEAR

09:09.298 --> 09:11.425
- Hey, Noa!
- Yes?

09:11.509 --> 09:13.886
You forgot your osechi.

09:14.428 --> 09:16.138
- Sorry. Thank you.
- There.

09:16.222 --> 09:17.765
- Thank you.
- Get home safe.

09:17.848 --> 09:18.683
- Okay.
- Bye.

09:18.766 --> 09:20.309
- Bye, everyone.
- Bye.

09:22.353 --> 09:23.688
We'll get going too.

09:23.771 --> 09:24.605
Okay.

09:24.689 --> 09:26.357
Thank you for the food, Shige.

09:26.440 --> 09:28.317
You're welcome. Go have fun.

09:37.076 --> 09:38.286
What?

09:41.581 --> 09:44.292
This is getting pretty old.

09:44.375 --> 09:49.422
‪TANOMI

09:49.505 --> 09:52.675
TOJO GENERAL HOSPITAL

09:59.348 --> 10:01.767
I come to this shrine every New Year's.

10:02.310 --> 10:03.561
Oh really?

10:03.644 --> 10:04.604
Yeah.

10:04.687 --> 10:07.523
HATSUMODE

10:11.819 --> 10:14.071
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

10:14.655 --> 10:15.948
Put it in here.

10:16.657 --> 10:18.826
Here we go. Ready…

10:31.547 --> 10:35.801
I pray that I can be true to myself

10:35.885 --> 10:38.721
and be with Taiga forever.

10:40.973 --> 10:44.226
I pray that I can be with Rin forever.

10:44.769 --> 10:47.688
Also, I pray that things work out well

10:47.772 --> 10:50.191
regarding my work and my goals.

10:50.274 --> 10:51.734
Also, I pray that

10:52.276 --> 10:56.197
my family, Rin, Rin's family,
and the people around me

10:56.280 --> 10:59.200
all enjoy good health
and live a happy life.

10:59.742 --> 11:02.495
I'm sorry for asking for so many things.

11:02.578 --> 11:05.623
Oh, but also, I pray that
everything goes smoothly.

11:05.706 --> 11:09.418
Thank you very much!
My name is Hase Taiga!

11:23.432 --> 11:26.102
I'm sorry. I asked for a lot of things.

11:27.019 --> 11:28.396
FORTUNE

11:28.479 --> 11:30.564
HATSUMODE

11:30.648 --> 11:32.733
- I'll pick mine now.
- Okay.

11:39.990 --> 11:41.700
- Ready…
- Ready…

11:45.788 --> 11:46.997
How mediocre.

11:47.081 --> 11:48.457
Blessings…

11:48.541 --> 11:49.417
Huh?

11:49.500 --> 11:50.835
It says I get blessings.

11:51.961 --> 11:54.922
That's better than me.
What does it say underneath?

11:56.674 --> 11:58.092
Give me a second…

12:02.388 --> 12:04.682
YOUR FORTUNE

12:04.765 --> 12:09.061
It says that my wishes will come true.

12:10.062 --> 12:11.188
That's great!

12:11.689 --> 12:12.940
Let me see.

12:13.023 --> 12:14.150
No.

12:14.233 --> 12:15.609
Why not?

12:15.693 --> 12:18.279
I'll take my time and read it
when I'm alone.

12:18.362 --> 12:20.406
Let's read it together now.

12:20.489 --> 12:21.407
- Come on!
- No.

12:21.490 --> 12:22.992
- Just a little.
- No!

12:23.075 --> 12:24.743
Just the first part.

12:27.746 --> 12:29.039
INTERNSHIP PROGRAM

12:39.300 --> 12:41.218
Hey!

12:41.302 --> 12:44.472
Taiga, I think it's time for a break.

12:45.014 --> 12:47.516
Okay. In a second.

12:48.559 --> 12:50.311
You're so studious, Taiga.

12:51.353 --> 12:53.939
Let's take a break already.

12:54.732 --> 12:57.026
Yeah… Just a second.

12:58.444 --> 13:00.779
Let's take a break.

13:01.322 --> 13:02.490
Hey, come on.

13:03.782 --> 13:04.909
- Hey!
- A break.

13:04.992 --> 13:06.118
Okay!

13:06.202 --> 13:07.620
- Let's take a break.
- Okay.

13:11.749 --> 13:15.753
Hey, you were so focused,
but what were you doing?

13:16.295 --> 13:19.215
Right now, I was looking at this.

13:20.257 --> 13:21.091
NEO MEAL JAPAN
REAL NUTRITION IN MEALS FOR ATHLETES

13:21.175 --> 13:24.011
"Meals for athletes…"

13:25.804 --> 13:29.725
It's a job that supports athletes
through food.

13:31.101 --> 13:34.396
I think I finally have an idea
of what my dream is.

13:34.980 --> 13:36.941
Although it took time to get here.

13:38.359 --> 13:39.944
Good for you, Taiga.

13:41.779 --> 13:43.322
It's all thanks to you.

13:45.741 --> 13:46.951
And so…

13:51.163 --> 13:52.831
I have something important to talk about.

13:55.167 --> 13:58.504
How long will your internship last?

14:00.965 --> 14:03.968
It'll end before I graduate.

14:04.051 --> 14:05.928
What will you do after that?

14:06.637 --> 14:09.348
I still don't know for sure.

14:10.975 --> 14:12.268
You know,

14:13.185 --> 14:16.897
I don't think it's right
to avoid this topic.

14:18.315 --> 14:21.902
So I want to face this issue properly.

14:24.530 --> 14:28.492
Once you graduate,
you have to return to Korea, right?

14:29.535 --> 14:31.287
You don't have a work visa, after all.

14:33.831 --> 14:36.500
Yeah, at this rate,
that's what will happen.

14:37.084 --> 14:38.335
Right…

14:39.044 --> 14:41.714
Unless you get hired
by a Japanese company,

14:42.423 --> 14:43.924
you have to go back.

14:44.425 --> 14:45.509
On top of that,

14:46.135 --> 14:49.388
you have to decide what you
want to become in the future,

14:49.471 --> 14:51.390
and work toward that goal,

14:52.600 --> 14:56.312
and think about whether or not
to stay with me.

14:57.354 --> 14:59.189
I'm sorry that I wasn't able

14:59.732 --> 15:02.109
to understand something so obvious.

15:02.985 --> 15:03.944
Don't worry.

15:05.988 --> 15:08.115
You've always been so kind to me.

15:10.701 --> 15:13.954
I still don't fully know
all of the difficulties you face.

15:15.497 --> 15:16.790
But I…

15:18.125 --> 15:22.129
want to stay with you
even after you graduate.

15:24.548 --> 15:25.674
So…

15:26.467 --> 15:28.719
I will do what I can, to make that happen.

15:29.637 --> 15:31.722
I'll make sure that we can
see each other regularly,

15:32.222 --> 15:34.016
no matter what you decide to do.

15:35.809 --> 15:38.520
To do that,
I'll learn to stand on my own two feet,

15:39.396 --> 15:40.898
even while chasing my dream.

15:44.818 --> 15:45.903
Taiga…

15:48.989 --> 15:50.491
In the end,

15:51.158 --> 15:53.619
I'm saying the same thing as before,
aren't I?

15:54.870 --> 15:58.666
I still don't have the guts to tell you
to stay in Japan.

15:59.208 --> 16:00.709
- But--
- It's not the same.

16:02.169 --> 16:03.379
It's totally different.

16:08.217 --> 16:09.718
I'm really happy.

16:10.761 --> 16:13.722
I want to be with you too.

16:16.141 --> 16:17.309
You do?

16:18.644 --> 16:22.147
I only have a little bit of time left,
but I'll do what I can.

16:29.405 --> 16:31.240
Noa, how are things with dongsaeng?

16:33.158 --> 16:34.243
Why all of a sudden?

16:35.619 --> 16:39.206
The thing is, he just contacted me
and said, "Let's go eat."

16:39.748 --> 16:41.333
What? I don't know about this.

16:41.417 --> 16:42.543
Go eat where?

16:43.502 --> 16:46.755
He said he wants to talk to me
about his future.

16:47.965 --> 16:49.466
Future?

16:50.426 --> 16:51.760
Akinori said that?

16:52.469 --> 16:53.637
Yes.

16:53.721 --> 16:56.015
It seems he is seriously

16:56.098 --> 16:58.142
thinking about a future with you.

17:01.061 --> 17:02.187
I see…

17:04.857 --> 17:06.358
As if!

17:06.442 --> 17:09.069
That was close! I almost fell for it.

17:12.197 --> 17:13.782
That was close…

17:25.919 --> 17:27.671
Ms. Park, do you have a moment?

17:28.505 --> 17:29.715
Yes?

17:29.798 --> 17:34.136
We're about to have a meeting
with a client, but I want you to join.

17:34.887 --> 17:37.181
- Me?
- Yes.

17:37.264 --> 17:41.518
Our client this time is
a Japanese subsidiary of a Korean company.

17:41.602 --> 17:43.020
I thought it's a good opportunity.

17:44.229 --> 17:46.482
- I would love to.
- Yeah?

17:47.107 --> 17:51.111
All that is left to discuss
is how to advertise the product.

17:51.737 --> 17:54.490
Do you have any requests
regarding the creative aspect?

17:54.573 --> 17:58.368
Yes, upon entering the Japanese market,
we would like to create

17:58.452 --> 18:01.455
a character IP that will catch
the attention of our target demographic.

18:01.538 --> 18:04.083
I see. Understood.

18:04.750 --> 18:06.335
Which means,

18:06.418 --> 18:09.254
the creative department
and illustrators will team up.

18:09.338 --> 18:10.547
How about

18:11.090 --> 18:15.302
we hold a contest within our company,
and choose from there?

18:15.886 --> 18:19.223
That sounds great. Let's go with that.

18:19.848 --> 18:21.558
Well then, thank you for your time.

18:21.642 --> 18:23.268
Thank you very much.

18:24.436 --> 18:25.729
- Good bye.
- Good bye.

18:31.610 --> 18:32.945
‪All right.

18:35.697 --> 18:37.324
- Ms. Hoshiumi.
- Yes?

18:39.827 --> 18:43.789
May I take part in the contest too?

18:45.624 --> 18:46.834
Well, of course.

18:47.626 --> 18:51.004
I'm looking for an open, fun idea.

18:52.673 --> 18:54.091
Thank you very much!

18:54.174 --> 18:55.634
You know,

18:55.717 --> 18:58.303
it's so nice that you
seized that opportunity yourself.

18:58.971 --> 19:00.597
Do your best.

19:02.307 --> 19:04.059
Yeah, thank you.

19:07.688 --> 19:10.107
I must say, your future looks so bright.

19:10.190 --> 19:13.902
It's a little blinding for me.
It's the beauty of youth.

19:14.570 --> 19:17.156
You and I are the same age.

19:17.239 --> 19:18.615
I know, but still.

19:19.283 --> 19:22.035
My life is going to stay the same forever.

19:22.953 --> 19:24.663
It's not going to change.

19:29.334 --> 19:32.796
Don't get the wrong idea.
I'm enjoying my life the way it is.

19:35.966 --> 19:38.218
I don't need my dreams to come true.

19:40.554 --> 19:42.514
Just working at this hotel,

19:43.223 --> 19:46.059
and watching guests
from all over the world

19:46.143 --> 19:50.063
makes me feel like I'm living overseas
and it's exciting.

19:50.856 --> 19:52.316
That's enough for me.

19:54.359 --> 19:57.779
Have you ever thought about
actually going overseas?

19:57.863 --> 19:59.573
There's no way I can.

20:00.532 --> 20:04.161
Why? I know you're studying English.

20:04.703 --> 20:07.080
You're working and have money too.

20:07.623 --> 20:11.210
No matter how much I make,
my mother and boyfriend use it all up.

20:11.293 --> 20:14.463
So it's not realistic.
You and I are different.

20:17.174 --> 20:19.593
If you really want to go overseas,

20:19.676 --> 20:22.179
just think about what you need to do
to make it happen.

20:23.597 --> 20:26.767
Must be nice to have been
raised in a privileged environment.

20:26.850 --> 20:29.853
Everyone should become
who they want to be.

20:29.937 --> 20:32.898
I'll think about it with you.
Let's share ideas. Okay?

20:34.816 --> 20:37.986
You are such a crazy princess.

20:38.946 --> 20:41.531
What the heck? Are you making fun of me?

20:42.324 --> 20:43.367
It's a compliment.

20:43.992 --> 20:45.869
I like that about you.

20:48.205 --> 20:49.915
- Let's hurry up and eat.
- Okay.

20:50.415 --> 20:51.250
TANOMI

20:51.333 --> 20:52.584
Closing Tanomi?

20:52.668 --> 20:53.543
Yeah.

20:53.627 --> 20:55.295
Nothing is official yet.

20:56.296 --> 20:59.383
I'm just saying that it's a possibility
we have to consider.

21:00.634 --> 21:02.386
Did something happen?

21:03.011 --> 21:06.807
I got a call from the hospital
saying my sister's condition isn't good.

21:07.391 --> 21:09.726
It can't be helped, you know?

21:11.561 --> 21:14.564
Come on, don't look so depressed.

21:14.648 --> 21:17.025
It's not like we're closing this instant.

21:20.320 --> 21:21.321
But…

21:22.239 --> 21:23.824
I'm sorry for making you worry.

21:24.366 --> 21:26.743
But what will be, will be.

21:29.913 --> 21:31.373
This may sound cliché,

21:32.124 --> 21:36.962
but you really can't take
what you have for granted.

21:37.504 --> 21:39.506
The older I get, the more I feel that way.

21:48.015 --> 21:49.224
I see.

21:49.766 --> 21:52.102
Thank you for sharing your thoughts.

21:52.185 --> 21:53.228
So you are looking

21:53.770 --> 21:56.898
for a job where you can
support athletes with your cooking?

21:56.982 --> 21:58.233
Yes.

21:59.026 --> 22:00.110
I…

22:00.861 --> 22:04.114
have been turning my eyes away
from the defeat

22:04.197 --> 22:06.241
I experienced in track
during my college days.

22:07.326 --> 22:08.952
I started cooking

22:09.578 --> 22:11.455
because I couldn't run as an athlete,

22:12.289 --> 22:14.499
and I had no other choice.

22:16.877 --> 22:17.961
But now,

22:19.087 --> 22:21.923
I genuinely feel a sense of accomplishment

22:22.841 --> 22:26.303
from this job,
where I can cook for others.

22:26.386 --> 22:27.763
Is that right?

22:28.346 --> 22:29.556
That's why

22:30.182 --> 22:33.310
I believe I can
make even better use of myself,

22:33.852 --> 22:36.354
if I can find a career
in making food for athletes.

22:36.438 --> 22:37.481
I see.

22:38.607 --> 22:41.401
And so, I did a lot of research

22:41.485 --> 22:44.571
and found that it takes four years
to become a registered dietitian.

22:45.155 --> 22:49.242
And even after that,
I need work experience to do anything…

22:49.785 --> 22:51.828
But you are in a hurry, right?

22:52.746 --> 22:53.830
Yes.

22:54.498 --> 22:56.750
I'd like to start working
as soon as possible.

23:00.837 --> 23:03.632
In that case,
you should get right into it.

23:05.342 --> 23:06.218
Huh?

23:07.636 --> 23:09.679
You can work for places like

23:10.263 --> 23:13.100
college dorms and company teams
with just a registration.

23:14.267 --> 23:15.602
Is that right?

23:16.478 --> 23:18.897
Why don't you just try it out?

23:20.273 --> 23:22.275
You can gain experience while working,

23:23.110 --> 23:25.153
and aim to become a sports dietitian.

23:26.029 --> 23:27.739
That's a valid option.

23:32.244 --> 23:33.411
Look.

23:34.746 --> 23:35.956
This one,

23:37.582 --> 23:38.667
and this one.

23:39.251 --> 23:41.419
They look pretty good, don't they?

23:42.963 --> 23:44.714
Well, doesn't someone look happy…

23:45.340 --> 23:46.842
You're really not coming back?

23:47.968 --> 23:49.094
I'm not.

23:49.177 --> 23:50.846
You're an idiot.

23:51.596 --> 23:55.267
Even if you can find a job in Japan,

23:55.350 --> 23:58.562
what if you break up in six months
or a year?

23:58.645 --> 24:00.105
You really won't regret this?

24:01.857 --> 24:02.899
I won't.

24:04.151 --> 24:08.822
Taiga treats me well,
so I want to stay with him.

24:09.489 --> 24:12.993
Jeez, you can gush about your boyfriend
all you want,

24:13.076 --> 24:15.120
but understand that I'm worried about you.

24:15.203 --> 24:16.580
Thank you.

24:16.663 --> 24:19.082
But I don't want to ignore
the way I'm feeling right now.

24:19.166 --> 24:22.836
Worrying about it
won't solve anything anyway.

24:22.919 --> 24:25.589
That might be right, but…

24:27.174 --> 24:29.801
You really don't need to worry.

24:29.885 --> 24:31.261
We won't break up.

24:33.013 --> 24:33.930
Please!

24:35.932 --> 24:38.143
So you just wanted money, huh?

24:39.728 --> 24:41.062
I'm sorry, hyeongnim.

24:42.689 --> 24:46.943
But I really want to pay
for Noa's mom's surgery.

24:48.778 --> 24:49.779
But…

24:51.573 --> 24:52.949
I have no money on hand.

24:54.201 --> 24:55.243
So…

24:56.203 --> 24:58.455
Please lend me some money.
I'll give it right back!

24:59.623 --> 25:01.917
Does Noa know about this?

25:02.918 --> 25:04.169
I'm keeping it a secret.

25:04.669 --> 25:06.671
I don't want her to feel bad about it.

25:13.345 --> 25:15.180
I will secretly work and pay you back.

25:15.263 --> 25:18.391
So please! Help cure Noa's mom's sickness!

25:18.475 --> 25:21.102
Hyeongnim, you're the only one I can ask!
Please!

25:24.731 --> 25:29.986
Forty-six, forty-seven, forty-eight,
forty-nine, fifty.

25:31.363 --> 25:32.614
It's all here.

25:33.281 --> 25:34.115
Okay.

25:34.199 --> 25:36.826
- All right then, I'll hold onto this.
- Okay.

25:37.327 --> 25:38.453
Um…

25:38.536 --> 25:41.581
With this,
I can definitely get the dividend, right?

25:42.123 --> 25:43.750
Of course!

25:43.833 --> 25:44.834
Good job.

25:45.961 --> 25:47.254
I'm so relieved!

25:47.337 --> 25:49.589
I worked really hard collecting
this money.

25:49.673 --> 25:51.841
I even cried
to my girlfriend's friends for help.

25:52.384 --> 25:54.427
You're brave, Akinori!

25:55.345 --> 25:58.390
Here, this is your first dividend.

25:58.473 --> 25:59.557
Wow, really?

26:00.475 --> 26:02.602
You'd better be grateful.

26:03.228 --> 26:05.563
This is what you'll be getting
every month.

26:05.647 --> 26:07.691
200,000 a month, huh?

26:07.774 --> 26:11.027
This is awesome! Amazing!

26:11.111 --> 26:13.780
In three months,
you will have made a profit of 100,000.

26:13.863 --> 26:16.032
From there, you'll just keep
receiving 200,000 a month.

26:18.034 --> 26:21.204
Zaki! Thank you for letting me in on this!

26:21.288 --> 26:23.039
Don't worry about it!

26:23.123 --> 26:25.375
I want my friends to live a good life.

26:27.002 --> 26:28.044
Thanks!

26:28.795 --> 26:31.381
- All right, then! I'll be leaving now!
- See you.

26:31.464 --> 26:32.632
Yes!

26:34.134 --> 26:35.302
Yes!

26:36.386 --> 26:37.595
What an idiot.

26:43.226 --> 26:44.477
Excuse me.

26:44.561 --> 26:47.731
I'm Hase. I called earlier.
I'm here to receive a pamphlet.

26:47.814 --> 26:49.357
One moment please.

27:27.479 --> 27:29.314
- This smells amazing.
- Sorry to make you wait.

27:29.397 --> 27:30.273
Hey.

27:32.901 --> 27:34.277
You bought more things?

27:34.819 --> 27:35.820
Yeah.

27:36.529 --> 27:38.531
What do you think? Isn't it cool?

27:40.116 --> 27:41.368
Yeah, sure.

27:47.415 --> 27:48.249
Here.

27:48.333 --> 27:49.459
Thank you for everything.

27:50.001 --> 27:50.877
Huh?

27:53.254 --> 27:55.632
You seem to be living large these days.

27:56.174 --> 27:57.801
Where did you get this money?

27:57.884 --> 28:00.887
I'm earning it through investments.

28:02.472 --> 28:05.225
Investment?
Don't you need money to invest first?

28:05.308 --> 28:06.393
Where did you get that?

28:06.476 --> 28:07.894
I borrowed it.

28:07.977 --> 28:09.854
- From who?
- A friend.

28:09.938 --> 28:11.231
Which friend?

28:11.940 --> 28:14.025
Just a friend.

28:17.862 --> 28:19.823
Tell me who you borrowed it from.

28:19.906 --> 28:21.032
Huh?

28:21.783 --> 28:24.702
- Who cares about that?
- Just tell me!

28:26.496 --> 28:28.498
Why are you all mad?

28:29.624 --> 28:33.753
I know I'm always troubling you,
so this time I got the money myself.

28:34.462 --> 28:36.256
- Why can't you be happy--
- I would rather

28:36.339 --> 28:37.298
you bother me than other people!

28:37.382 --> 28:38.508
Just tell me!

28:40.051 --> 28:41.261
I'm sorry.

28:41.344 --> 28:42.470
Sorry about that.

28:43.513 --> 28:46.516
Hey, don't get so mad!

28:50.019 --> 28:52.063
It was Jun-ho.

28:53.732 --> 28:56.818
- You really--
- I can pay him back right away.

28:57.318 --> 29:01.072
I already got my 200,000 dividend
and I don't need to pay anymore.

29:01.156 --> 29:02.449
Now I just get 200,000 every month--

29:02.532 --> 29:05.201
Obviously that's too good to be true!
Are you an idiot?!

29:05.285 --> 29:06.745
It's true!

29:09.164 --> 29:11.833
I'll be getting a steady income.

29:12.500 --> 29:13.543
Then,

29:14.085 --> 29:16.546
we'll be able to rent a place
and live together.

29:19.924 --> 29:22.385
Have a little faith in me, will you?

29:29.851 --> 29:31.603
Let's go apologize to Jun-ho.

29:33.980 --> 29:35.732
- What?
- I said, let's go!

29:45.325 --> 29:46.785
I'm really sorry.

29:47.702 --> 29:48.745
Hyeongnim…

29:49.996 --> 29:51.289
I'm sorry.

29:52.123 --> 29:55.293
- I didn't mean to trick you--
- This isn't your time to make excuses.

29:56.628 --> 29:58.171
We're only here to apologize.

29:58.254 --> 29:59.756
I was going to return it double.

29:59.839 --> 30:02.258
- But--
- It's too good to be true.

30:02.342 --> 30:03.676
You're so stupid.

30:04.385 --> 30:06.054
I said, I'm sorry.

30:06.596 --> 30:07.972
How stupid can you be?

30:09.224 --> 30:10.892
It's almost sad.

30:13.353 --> 30:15.647
I knew you were stupid,
but this is a new low.

30:15.730 --> 30:17.482
Stop calling me stupid.

30:17.565 --> 30:20.735
- I wanted to change too, you know?
- Then why did you borrow money?

30:20.819 --> 30:22.487
You need money to change!

30:22.570 --> 30:23.988
Just apologize already!

30:24.072 --> 30:25.198
Enough!

30:27.325 --> 30:28.284
Dongsaeng,

30:29.202 --> 30:30.829
I lent you money

30:31.538 --> 30:33.623
because I trusted you as a person.

30:38.795 --> 30:40.380
This is Noa's money, isn't it?

30:41.965 --> 30:43.258
Then I can't accept it.

30:45.927 --> 30:46.970
You need to pay me yourself.

30:48.346 --> 30:49.639
I trust you.

31:04.279 --> 31:07.365
That kind of attitude
is the most annoying.

31:09.242 --> 31:10.285
Huh?

31:12.120 --> 31:13.580
Are you serious?

31:14.914 --> 31:17.625
Do you not understand
how kind he is being?

31:17.709 --> 31:21.087
You guys just look down on me, that's all.

31:22.839 --> 31:26.009
You trusted me of your own will,
and now you're disappointed.

31:27.552 --> 31:29.095
It's so annoying.

31:30.263 --> 31:32.473
Hey… Hey!

31:32.557 --> 31:35.059
Move. Hey…

31:39.230 --> 31:40.273
Please…

31:43.985 --> 31:45.111
Apologize.

32:09.886 --> 32:11.304
I'm sorry, Jun-ho.

32:16.601 --> 32:17.727
This is…

32:19.479 --> 32:20.355
too much…

32:37.538 --> 32:38.915
You don't need to worry.

32:43.670 --> 32:44.671
That…

32:47.340 --> 32:48.633
Will you please accept it?

32:53.179 --> 32:54.931
I lent money to him, not you.

33:03.064 --> 33:06.985
So what are you going to do
about your boyfriend?

33:24.252 --> 33:25.878
I guess it's over.

33:27.839 --> 33:29.841
There's no future with him.

33:34.804 --> 33:35.847
Noa…

33:37.515 --> 33:38.808
Thank you.

33:42.353 --> 33:43.563
You know how…

33:45.314 --> 33:46.774
you told me before…

33:49.235 --> 33:50.903
that I should become who I want to be?

33:52.655 --> 33:53.740
Yeah.

34:03.541 --> 34:06.127
If I stay with him,
I don't think I'll ever change.

34:11.507 --> 34:12.842
I see.

34:24.062 --> 34:25.104
Rin…

34:29.525 --> 34:30.693
I can do this, right?

34:35.490 --> 34:38.284
If that is what you truly wish to do,

34:39.118 --> 34:42.955
I will support that decision,
no matter what it is.

34:52.965 --> 34:54.342
Thank you.

34:58.346 --> 34:59.222
You're so nice…

35:12.527 --> 35:14.112
I'm sorry about everything.

35:15.238 --> 35:17.907
It's fine. What's done is done.

35:21.369 --> 35:22.662
Hey…

35:24.914 --> 35:28.709
What about all the money
I've borrowed from you?

35:30.002 --> 35:31.254
It's fine.

35:32.630 --> 35:34.215
Think of it as settlement money.

35:35.424 --> 35:38.719
More like, can you even pay me back
if I asked for it?

35:47.854 --> 35:48.938
I can't.

35:49.522 --> 35:51.482
Don't corner me like that on our last day.

36:02.869 --> 36:04.829
You didn't forget anything, right?

36:04.912 --> 36:06.873
No, I don't think so.

36:13.296 --> 36:14.380
Bye.

36:14.922 --> 36:17.175
What? You're not seeing me off?

36:17.884 --> 36:20.970
Why would I? Don't be a baby.

36:24.515 --> 36:25.516
Okay.

36:33.149 --> 36:34.150
Bye.

36:36.235 --> 36:37.528
Akinori.

36:41.365 --> 36:42.783
It was fun.

36:45.828 --> 36:47.830
Living like a bum with you.

36:51.918 --> 36:53.169
What the heck?

37:35.294 --> 37:36.545
All right…

37:39.674 --> 37:41.801
I sent in a few applications.

37:41.884 --> 37:44.470
But I haven't done an entrance exam
in so long, I'm so nervous.

37:45.263 --> 37:48.224
Maybe I'll go to a shrine
and pray that I get accepted.

37:48.766 --> 37:50.226
You'll be fine, Taiga.

37:51.060 --> 37:52.603
I need to do my best too.

37:54.397 --> 37:56.065
I'll get back to work now.

37:56.649 --> 37:59.402
Oh, sorry. Do your best.

37:59.986 --> 38:02.321
I will. Taiga, you can do it too.

38:07.201 --> 38:08.703
Shrine…

38:10.997 --> 38:13.499
I'll take my time and read it
when I'm alone.

38:24.593 --> 38:26.304
I'll lose something big?

38:33.019 --> 38:36.397
Going into the advertising industry now?
There's no way you'll succeed!

38:36.480 --> 38:38.482
You've been suffocating me like that
this whole time.

38:38.566 --> 38:40.109
Can you please translate

38:40.693 --> 38:42.945
what I'm going to say to your mother?

38:43.029 --> 38:43.863
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
